<mxCell id="lg_color_t" value="Blue: core, spine · Green: leaf · Orange: router · Red: firewall · Pink: load balancer · Gray: external domain, controller, management server, workloads. Dashed boxes: Digital Map regions (access regions: Extranet, Internet, WAN; core region; service resource region: Fabric zone)." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="legend">
  <mxGeometry x="16" y="34" width="1408" height="20" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="lg_note_t" value="Data center 2 has the same topology as Data center 1, drawn mirrored. One border-leaf pair carries both the DMZ and DC tenants; the DC firewall is off-path. Each domain controller manages its whole fabric. The FortiGate is an HTTP proxy for branch terminals and has no link to the branches. The FPR-2140 to core link is out of POC scope." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="legend">
  <mxGeometry x="16" y="58" width="1408" height="30" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
